    "ff_fitment_guide_g8x": {
      "type": "ff-fitment-guide",
      "blocks": {
        "tier_daily": {
          "type": "tier",
          "settings": {
            "tier_title": "Daily Street & OEM+ Bolt-On",
            "tier_intro": "<p>These bolt-on setups are ideal for enthusiasts enjoying their G8X day-to-day on the street, typically paired with all-season or performance-oriented summer tires. They improve the look and feel of the car without requiring modifications or changes to the factory alignment \u2014 just bolt on and enjoy.</p><p>While these fitments work fine for the occasional track day or AutoX, drivers chasing more performance should look at our Performance Street & Track or Hardcore Track & Race tiers below.</p>",
            "a_label": "Staggered",
            "a_front": "20x10 ET10",
            "a_rear": "20x11 ET12",
            "a_image": "shopify://shop_images/IMG_0537.jpg",
            "a_notes": "The go to OEM+ flush setup for the G8X chassis. The offset tucks the wheel in just enough for a clean, flush yet safe look while still maintaining strong concavity. Direct bolt-on stance  \u2014 no spacers needed.",
            "a_tire_pick": "Front: 285/30-20 // Rear: 295/30-20\u00a0",
            "a_tire_flags": "\u00b7X-Drive compatible",
            "a_tire_allseason": "Michelin Pilot Sport AS4 (540TW), Continental ExtremeContact DWS06+ (560TW)",
            "a_tire_uhp": "Falken Azenis FK510 (300TW), Firestone Firehawk Indy 500 (340TW)",
            "a_tire_max": "Michelin Pilot Sport 4S (300TW), Continental ExtremeContact Sport (340TW), Yokohama Advan Apex V601 (280TW)",
            "a_tire_extreme": "",
            "a_tire_rcompound": "",
            "a_tire_drag": "",
            "b_label": "Staggered",
            "b_front": "Front: 19x10\u201d ET10",
            "b_rear": "Rear: 20x10.5\u201d ET18",
            "b_image": "shopify://shop_images/IMG_0552.jpg",
            "b_notes": "A slightly narrower width and higher offset setup that keeps the wheels tucked in for a clean, OEM+ flush look with no poke. The 19\" front improves steering feel and ride quality, while the 20\" adds traction and a subtle bump in concavity. Direct bolt-on fitment that prioritizes drivability.\n\n(Works with OEM tires)",
            "b_tire_pick": "Front 275/35-19 // Rear 285/30-20",
            "b_tire_flags": "X-Drive compatible",
            "b_tire_allseason": "Continental ExtremeContact DWS06+ (560TW), Michelin Pilot Sport AS4 (540TW)",
            "b_tire_uhp": "Firestone Firehawk Indy 500 (340TW), Falken Azenis FK510 (300TW)",
            "b_tire_max": "Michelin Pilot Sport 4S (300TW), Continental ExtremeContact Sport (340TW), Yokohama Advan Apex V601 (280TW), Pirelli P Zero (220TW)",
            "b_tire_extreme": "",
            "b_tire_rcompound": "",
            "b_tire_drag": ""
          }
        },
        "tier_aggressive": {
          "type": "tier",
          "settings": {
            "tier_title": "Aggressive Street",
            "tier_intro": "<p>Aggressive fitments focused on appearance \u2014 ideal for the driver who wants to fill the wheel wells with wider rubber and near-flush offsets. These setups are typically still a direct bolt-on, but some combinations benefit from a light spacer or a touch of negative camber to dial in the perfect blend of form and function. Narrower relative tire widths help move the sidewall away from the fender at more aggressive offsets \u2014 street-oriented all-season and summer tires are the most popular pairing here.</p>",
            "a_label": "Staggered",
            "a_front": "20x10 ET12",
            "a_rear": "20x11 ET10",
            "a_image": "shopify://shop_images/IMG_7936.jpg",
            "a_notes": "Aggressive, flush fitment for the G8X chassis. Wider widths combined with lower offsets push the wheels outward to sit nearly even with the fenders, creating a strong, planted stance with maximum concavity. Direct bolt-on with no spacers needed, though proper tire sizing may be required for a perfectly dialed-in look.",
            "a_tire_pick": "Front 275/35-20 // Rear 305/30-20",
            "a_tire_flags": "X-Drive compatible \u00b7 some front rubbing can occur against the inner fender liner at full steering lock",
            "a_tire_allseason": "",
            "a_tire_uhp": "Falken Azenis FK510 (300TW), Firestone Firehawk Indy 500 (340TW)",
            "a_tire_max": "Michelin Pilot Sport 4S (300TW), Continental ExtremeContact Sport (340TW), Bridgestone Potenza Sport (300TW)",
            "a_tire_extreme": "Goodyear Eagle F1 Supercar 3 (220TW)",
            "a_tire_rcompound": "",
            "a_tire_drag": "",
            "b_label": "Staggered (mixed diameter)",
            "b_front": "19x10 ET12",
            "b_rear": "20x11 ET10",
            "b_image": "shopify://shop_images/IMG_0546.jpg",
            "b_notes": "Aggressive, performance-focused staggered fitment. The 19\" front allows for better steering response, a lighter feel, and improved ride comfort, while the wider 20\" rear increases rear grip and delivers a deeper concave profile. A balanced combination of daily drivability and enhanced traction \u2014 no spacers required.",
            "b_tire_pick": "Front 275/35-19 // Rear 305/30-20",
            "b_tire_flags": "Some front rubbing can occur against the inner fender liner at full steering lock",
            "b_tire_allseason": "",
            "b_tire_uhp": "Falken Azenis FK510 (300TW)",
            "b_tire_max": "Michelin Pilot Sport 4S (300TW), Continental ExtremeContact Sport (340TW), Hankook Ventus V12 Evo2 (320TW)",
            "b_tire_extreme": "Michelin Pilot Sport Cup 2 Connect (240TW)",
            "b_tire_rcompound": "",
            "b_tire_drag": ""
          }
        },
        "tier_performance": {
          "type": "tier",
          "settings": {
            "tier_title": "Performance Street & Track",
            "tier_intro": "<p>Whether you enjoy spirited street driving or you're a weekend track warrior chasing lap times, these wheel and tire configurations deliver a more dramatic step up in performance \u2014 typically paired with performance-oriented summer tires or track-oriented R-compounds.</p><p>Many of these fitments can be run on the factory alignment, but if you plan to track the car we highly recommend dialing in extra negative camber to improve handling and get the most life and grip out of your tires.</p>",
            "a_label": "SQUARED",
            "a_front": "19x10 ET12",
            "a_rear": "19x10 ET12",
            "a_image": "shopify://shop_images/IMG_0539.jpg",
            "a_notes": "An aggressive, track-inspired fitment. Running 19s all around keeps overall weight lower and improves ride compliance, ideal for spirited driving or performance use. The ET12 front sits near flush with a purposeful, planted look.",
            "a_tire_pick": "Front 275/35-19 // Rear 295/35-19",
            "a_tire_uhp": "Falken Azenis FK510 (300TW)",
            "a_tire_max": "Michelin Pilot Sport 4S (300TW), Continental ExtremeContact Sport (340TW), Pirelli P Zero (220TW)",
            "a_tire_extreme": "Falken Azenis RT660 (200TW)",
            "a_tire_rcompound": "Michelin Pilot Sport Cup 2 (180TW)"
          }
        },
        "tier_drag": {
          "type": "tier",
          "settings": {
            "tier_title": "Drag Race",
            "tier_intro": "<p>For maximum straight-line traction and the lowest ETs. This tier pairs a standard front wheel with a Fortune Forged beadlock rear pair for confident traction under heavy load. Not recommended in cold or wet conditions.</p>",
            "a_label": "Beadlock rear pair",
            "a_front": "",
            "a_rear": "18x11 ET15",
            "a_image": "shopify://shop_images/IMG_6681.jpg",
            "a_notes": "The ideal drag-focused fitment for the G8X chassis. The 18\" beadlock rear pair sits properly within the fender at ET15 for a clean, planted look and remains a direct bolt-on with no clearance issues \u2014 designed for maximum straight-line traction. Pair with any Fortune Forged front wheel design; no spacers needed.",
            "a_tire_pick": "Front 275/35-19 // Rear 305/35-18",
